* Test circuit for the solver's MOSFET (tools/spice/cases/cmos.py; docs/circuit/solver-mosfet.md),
* not a part of the TR-909: a ring of three 4069UB inverters on the supply vdd, each into 47k and
* 22 nF to ground (the next one's gate): an audio-rate oscillator, about 300 Hz at 5 V, whose
* inverters pass through their linear region at every edge. Its DC point (every node at the
* inverters' threshold) is unstable; the input kick, a current into the first stage's
* capacitor, leaves it the same way in the solver and in ngspice.
* Inputs: vdd (volts), kick (amps). Outputs: a (the first stage's capacitor), o1 (its inverter).
Vdd vdd 0 input vdd
Ik 0 a input kick
MP1 o1 c vdd 4069UB_P
MN1 o1 c 0 4069UB_N
R1 o1 a 47k
C1 a 0 22n
MP2 o2 a vdd 4069UB_P
MN2 o2 a 0 4069UB_N
R2 o2 b 47k
C2 b 0 22n
MP3 o3 b vdd 4069UB_P
MN3 o3 b 0 4069UB_N
R3 o3 c 47k
C3 c 0 22n
.output a a
.output o1 o1
